Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Configure xs-fcoe with the fcoe-utils of EL10

The fcoe-utils of EL10 has its configuration, SUPPORTED_DRIVERS, in
/etc/fcoe/config, rather than in /etc/sysconfig/fcoe, which it no longer
ships: without it, xs-fcoe failed at boot. And its drivers include some
the kernel may not have, like qedf: their modprobe failing fails it no
more, the others still loaded.
---
 src/common/usr/lib/systemd/system/xs-fcoe.service | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/common/usr/lib/systemd/system/xs-fcoe.service b/src/common/usr/lib/systemd/system/xs-fcoe.service
index bf9b2d1..1bfedae 100644
--- a/src/common/usr/lib/systemd/system/xs-fcoe.service
+++ b/src/common/usr/lib/systemd/system/xs-fcoe.service
@@ -4,8 +4,8 @@
 
 [Service]
 Type=oneshot
-EnvironmentFile=/etc/sysconfig/fcoe
-ExecStartPre=/sbin/modprobe -qa $SUPPORTED_DRIVERS
+EnvironmentFile=/etc/fcoe/config
+ExecStartPre=-/sbin/modprobe -qa $SUPPORTED_DRIVERS
 ExecStart=/opt/xensource/libexec/fcoe_driver --init
 
 [Install]
-- 
2.47.3

